This fixture is synthetic. It was hand-authored for the Inflight reachability
test harness and does not represent output captured from a real AWS account.

It models a single-instance web tier: one VPC, one subnet, one EC2 instance
(i-web00000000000001), and one security group (sg-web000000000001) carrying
two world-open ingress rules, each a single-port rule sourced from
0.0.0.0/0:

  - tcp/22  (SSH)  from 0.0.0.0/0  -- Checkov CKV_AWS_24 (open SSH)
  - tcp/3389 (RDP) from 0.0.0.0/0  -- Checkov CKV_AWS_25 (open RDP)

The SSH rule is declared first in IpPermissions (synthesized rule id
sg-web000000000001-in-0-0.0.0.0/0) and the RDP rule second (synthesized rule
id sg-web000000000001-in-1-0.0.0.0/0), per snapshot_describe's
{sg_id}-in-{index}-{cidr} scheme. The field shapes were copied from the
tests/fixtures/aws/two-tier fixture (itself derived from vendored real AWS
describe-* output), then simplified and rewritten with fabricated
identifiers, so it loads correctly under Inflight's describe-dir loader.
Every VPC id, subnet id, instance id, security group id, ENI id, IP address,
and account id in this fixture is fabricated for this purpose.

Do not treat any value in this directory as real infrastructure.
